# nr-office-pdf-adapter: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own)
# Written without cargo: none of the new modules of mixdog-office-pdf has been compiled or run in Rust (the recording was
# produced by running Node over generated PDFs; rustfmt parsed every Rust file of the task).

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/src/lib.rs
Add, right after `pub mod analysis;`:

    pub mod adapter;
    pub mod edit_document;
    pub mod safety;
    pub mod security;
    pub mod structure;

(The crate's other tasks add their own `pub mod` lines the same way.) Optional single-import re-exports for the tool
layer, after the existing `pub use` lines:

    pub use adapter::{
        BatchState, FormView, OperationSet, PDF_AUDIT_MAX_CHARS, SnapshotOptions, apply_pdf_batch, issues_pdf,
        snapshot_pdf, validate_pdf,
    };
    pub use edit_document::{PDF_ENCRYPTED_HINT, load_pdf, page_spin, pdf_attachments, selected_edit_pages, write_sibling};
    pub use safety::active_content_issues;
    pub use security::{SecureRequest, qpdf_available, secure_pdf};
    pub use structure::StructureOperations;

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/Cargo.toml (the crate's own manifest; not in this task's files)
[dependencies]: add (all already in native/core/Cargo.lock; no new crate enters the lock):

    mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-ooxml = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "time", "process", "io-util"] }
    uuid = { workspace = true, features = ["v4"] }

[dev-dependencies] keeps `mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true, features = ["test-support"] }` and `mixdog-testkit`.
Why: `mixdog-office-base` for `write_note::WriteNote` (the call's note of every file written; it was a dev-dependency
only), `mixdog-ooxml` for `placeholder_scan::placeholder_text_issues` (one list for every format with visible text; the
ooxml crate does not depend on this one, so there is no cycle), `mixdog-rt` + `tokio` for the bounded qpdf run
(`mixdog_rt::time::timeout` over `tokio::process`, the spawn route the lint allows; std::process::Command is banned),
`uuid` for the temporary names of the response file and the sibling of a file secured in place.
Cargo.lock: the package `mixdog-office-pdf` gains those five entries in its dependency list.

## 3. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
Index the new set `office-adapter` (recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-adapter.mjs, 1 file,
golden.json; the set's own MANIFEST.json is at native/core/fixtures/office-adapter/MANIFEST.json) with the manifest tool
that built the other entries: `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index`.

## 4. SERVICE_PENDING (mixdog-app-server-daemon compose_flip.rs)
Nothing to remove: this task registers no protocol method, no service and no tool. The tool surface that calls these
functions is another task's.

## 5. Seams the lead connects after the wave (each is a trait this task defines and another task implements)
- `adapter::FormView` (describe_fields, minimum_size, rectangles_overlap) is implemented by the forms module of
  nr-office-pdf-forms over `describeFormField`, `minimumFieldSize` and `rectanglesOverlap`. The snapshot lists the form
  through it and the audit's unnamed_form_field / field_too_small / overlapping_form_fields issues read its answers.
- `adapter::OperationSet` is implemented by `structure::StructureOperations` (this task) and by the content operations
  (nr-office-pdf-content-ops: fill, draw, marks, flatten, ocr, ...; the mark operations answer `keeps_measurement`
  true, as `MARK_OPERATIONS` did). The caller of `apply_pdf_batch` passes both: `&[&content, &StructureOperations]`.
  `BatchState.document` is replaceable by a handler that must continue on a fresh load; `BatchState.measure` carries
  what a mark measured (a boxed value of the content module's own type).

## 6. Consumers
`mixdog_office_pdf::adapter::{snapshot_pdf, validate_pdf, issues_pdf, apply_pdf_batch}` (blocking, generic over the
read/write lane proof, as the analysis functions are; options through `SnapshotOptions::from_json`),
`edit_document::{load_pdf, selected_edit_pages, pdf_attachments, write_sibling, page_spin, PDF_ENCRYPTED_HINT}`,
`safety::active_content_issues`, `security::{secure_pdf, qpdf_available}`. `secure_pdf` starts qpdf on a runtime of its
own and so is for a lane job (a plain thread), never for a runtime worker; it needs the call's `WriteNote`.

## 7. Tests
tests/twin_adapter.rs (replays native/core/fixtures/office-adapter/golden.json; `twin_live_adapter` is #[ignore]),
tests/security.rs (no qpdf, no process), and unit tests in adapter.rs, edit_document.rs and safety.rs.

## 8. Not covered by the recording
qpdf itself (not installed here, and a recording must not depend on it); an encrypted file's snapshot (making one needs
qpdf); the form descriptions (the forms module's twin).
